"The postoperative pathology reveals a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological stage pT3a, with extraprostatic extension documented. Reassuring findings include negative surgical margins and no invasion of the seminal vesicles, as stated in the surgical pathology report: \"surgical margins were negative; the seminal vesicles were not invaded.\" However, lymphovascular invasion was present, and no lymph nodes were removed. Biopsy findings showed Gleason 3+3 and 3+4, with no cribriform pattern, intraductal carcinoma, or perineural invasion noted. The absence of documented postoperative PSA means biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. The status of nodal sampling is unknown, and pNx does not establish node-negative disease, which widens uncertainty regarding regional disease control. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory is crucial for revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 50.59 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 32.89–68.30 months; its coverage has not been validated."
